# Session Guide

Load this file at the start of every `/{{name}}` session. It covers intake,
context gathering, and the adaptive interview that produces the work specification.

---

## Step 1 — Orientation

Open with an orientation block (blockquote):

> Welcome. This {{skill_type}} works with {{subject_description}}. No specialized
> background needed.
>
> Steps overview:
> - Step 1: Orientation (this step)
> - Step 2: Context — what is being {{verb_past_participle}} and who is the audience
> - Step 3: Materials — gather the inputs
> - Step 4: Adaptive interview — agree scope, bounds, and quality criteria
> - Step 5: Execution — perform the {{skill_type}}
> - Step 6: Verification — run automated checks
> - Step 7: Report — generate deliverables
> - Step 8: Handoff — save, explain findings, suggest next steps
>
> Most sessions take {{estimated_duration}}.

Final line: "You can update or correct anything at any time — just tell me.
Ready? Let's start."

